WEBVTT

gender-05-1
00:00:01.100 --> 00:00:04.180
“I love gentle women.”

gender-05-2
00:00:04.180 --> 00:00:06.420
“I don't want to go today.”

gender-05-3
00:00:06.420 --> 00:00:08.860
“Why have you changed?”

gender-05-4
00:00:08.860 --> 00:00:14.360
He loves women. But which kind?

gender-05-5
00:00:15.660 --> 00:00:21.790
Episode 5: He loves women. Why might he
still be a misogynist?

gender-05-6
00:00:22.990 --> 00:00:28.110
Imagine a weekend dinner at her
boyfriend's parents' home.

gender-05-7
00:00:28.110 --> 00:00:31.170
“Look how well she looks after everyone.”

gender-05-8
00:00:31.170 --> 00:00:34.890
“Such a good homemaker. Our family will
be lucky to have her.”

gender-05-9
00:00:34.890 --> 00:00:40.150
When she complies, the praise keeps
coming.

gender-05-10
00:00:41.250 --> 00:00:45.780
“I'd like to leave early. I have a report
due tomorrow.”

gender-05-11
00:00:45.780 --> 00:00:47.820
“You just got here, and you're leaving?”

gender-05-12
00:00:47.820 --> 00:00:51.090
“Can't you help me save face?”

gender-05-13
00:00:51.090 --> 00:00:57.529
The same man, the same woman. She is
praised for complying; when she refuses,

gender-05-14
00:00:57.529 --> 00:00:58.950
she pays a price.

gender-05-15
00:01:00.050 --> 00:01:04.830
Liking certain women: those who care for
others, give way and cooperate.

gender-05-16
00:01:04.830 --> 00:01:09.180
Accepting women's independent wishes:
including when she says “no.”

gender-05-17
00:01:09.180 --> 00:01:12.230
These can be entirely separate things.

gender-05-18
00:01:12.230 --> 00:01:17.970
The woman who says “no” is outside the
scope of that affection.

gender-05-19
00:01:19.070 --> 00:01:23.730
Philosopher Kate Manne divides this into
two parts.

gender-05-20
00:01:23.730 --> 00:01:28.954
Sexism is like an instruction manual: it
justifies assigned roles. “Women are

gender-05-21
00:01:28.954 --> 00:01:31.600
naturally better at caring for others.”

gender-05-22
00:01:31.600 --> 00:01:37.495
Misogyny is like an enforcer: follow the
manual and be rewarded; refuse, and be

gender-05-23
00:01:37.495 --> 00:01:38.390
made to pay.

gender-05-24
00:01:38.390 --> 00:01:40.904
Kate Manne, Down Girl: The Logic of
Misogyny (2017): sexism justifies

gender-05-25
00:01:40.904 --> 00:01:42.580
patriarchy; misogyny enforces it.
(Paraphrase)

gender-05-26
00:01:42.580 --> 00:01:47.886
So misogyny need not mean hating all
women. It is more like a system of

gender-05-27
00:01:47.886 --> 00:01:49.530
rewards and penalties.

gender-05-28
00:01:53.130 --> 00:01:58.951
Expect care and deference → her response
→ praise or penalties → the expectation

gender-05-29
00:01:58.951 --> 00:01:59.970
is reinforced.

gender-05-30
00:01:59.970 --> 00:02:04.629
The penalties need not come from one
person: a partner's displeasure, a

gender-05-31
00:02:04.629 --> 00:02:07.450
relative's remark, a label in a group
chat.

gender-05-32
00:02:07.450 --> 00:02:16.840
Pause: what praise of women have you
heard that came with conditions?

gender-05-33
00:02:17.940 --> 00:02:22.480
A boundary: not all criticism of women is
misogyny.

gender-05-34
00:02:22.480 --> 00:02:27.100
“This figure in your report is wrong.”
That criticizes her work.

gender-05-35
00:02:27.100 --> 00:02:32.660
“So pushy, for a woman.” That defends the
rule that women should give way.

gender-05-36
00:02:32.660 --> 00:02:37.400
Ask: which gender norm is this criticism
defending?

gender-05-37
00:02:37.400 --> 00:02:45.532
And women who follow the rules can be
harmed too. Their praise is part of the

gender-05-38
00:02:45.532 --> 00:02:46.060
cage.

gender-05-39
00:02:47.160 --> 00:02:51.310
To judge someone's “affection,” don't
count the compliments.

gender-05-40
00:02:51.310 --> 00:02:58.040
Ask: who does this affection allow her to
become?

gender-05-41
00:02:59.140 --> 00:03:01.980
Next time, we keep asking:

gender-05-42
00:03:01.980 --> 00:03:08.060
Can feminism rest on just one kind of
female experience?

gender-05-43
00:03:10.360 --> 00:03:15.260
This is UjiBricks.
